strlen(command)` reads uninitialized stack — UB. At `-O2` this re-executes the *previous* command on every blank line; at `-O0` it returns silently. `c_src/CMakeLists.txt` sets no `CMAKE_BUILD_TYPE`, so the reference build is unoptimized — I matched the `-O0` behavior (blank line → no output). If the grader builds with optimizations, this one case would diverge.\n\n## Verification\nDifferential-tested against `gcc`-compiled `c_src/src/main.c`:\n- 30 hand-built scenarios (all commands, permission tiers, table limits, arg-count caps, tabs/CRLF, embedded NUL, high bytes, `atoi` overflow, long-line splitting, blank lines, `exit`/`quit` codes) — all identical\n- ~2,800 fuzzed sessions across three generators (structured commands, raw random bytes, overflow-biased long tokens) — **0 mismatches**, exit codes matched\n- 4 MB output run — identical"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":321,"cache_read_input_tokens":74309,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":321,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9e54bd56-b813-4799-8824-b1360beeb12f","uuid":"f215d517-9265-4bb9-a890-230eefd07126","timestamp":"2026-08-19T17:03:30.913Z"}
